WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.550
No matter how much we may look forward to
new episodes of our favorite shows, there's

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:09.099
no such thing as a perfect TV series - and
even the most popular and critically acclaimed

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.519
small-screen hits have made some really, really
awful choices.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.920
The entire sixth season of The Walking Dead
led up to one moment.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.650
Comic fans had already broken the news to
TV viewers: Glenn would die beneath the bloody

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.180
baseball bat of Negan, leader of the Saviors.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.760
As the season entered its final moments, though,
all we got was... well, this:

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.320
"You can breathe.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.780
You can blink.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.700
You can cry.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.720
Hell, you're all gonna be doing that."

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.040
Basically, it was the world's least satisfying
cliffhanger.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.200
Did Glenn die?

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.240
Or did somebody else find themselves at the
business end of Lucille?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.480
Was it someone we even cared about?

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:53.340
The showrunners defended the non-reveal by
saying it was done in the interest of storytelling,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.640
but it wouldn't have been quite so bad were
it not for a blunder earlier in the season.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:02.040
For a few episodes, Dead made a big deal about
Glenn being, well, dead.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:02.840
Which he wasn't.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.600
The zombie epic never had to fake us out about
mortality before, but the introduction of

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.040
goofy camera tricks had already left a rotten
taste in everyone's mouths.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.980
Just give us the gory goods - and a heaping
helping of the feels - or get out of the way.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.980
The writers of The Big Bang Theory have always
made the nerds the guys that you root for.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.000
Even if they make dumb mistakes, they're generally
not reprehensible jerks.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.580
Even Sheldon's obnoxious idiosyncrasies are
generally charming.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.520
And the romance between Leonard and Penny
is probably one of the sweeter things on TV,

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.960
so the eighth season finale was the ultimate
bummer.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:40.920
On their way to get married in Vegas, Leonard
admits to Penny that he'd kissed another girl,

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.960
gut-punching everyone in the audience who
believes in true love.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:44.840
"What did you do?"

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.660
"Nothing… really.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.340
It was just kissing."

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.030
Not only is it a weird hurdle to throw in
front of the characters, but it's also strangely

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.850
out of character for the show, which never
really gets heavier than the death of Howard's

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.000
mom - and that was more of a tribute to the
late actress Carol Ann Susi than a significant

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:01.500
plot point.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.760
Turning everynerd Leonard into a lech, and
making the audience marinate on it all summer

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.860
long, sucked.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.780
Why can't we just have nice things?

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.420
Friends was really about two things: the titular
friends hanging out with each other, and those

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.300
friends dating an endless parade of people
who weren't as good as their friends.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.580
To that end, two of the friends - Chandler
and Monica - married within the circle, while

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.470
Phoebe found love with Mike, who was able
to infiltrate the core group because he was

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.260
played by Paul Rudd, the most charming man
on Earth.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.800
Putting off that moment when they inevitably
got Ross and Rachel back together for good,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.310
Friends writers killed some time in the final
years of the show by trying to make Rachel

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.220
and Joey a thing.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.860
Let us repeat that again: Someone thought
it was a good idea to put this man …

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:41.940
Check it out, check it out.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.360
It's like it's coming right at me."

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.940
And this woman …

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.720
"You give me back my sweater or it's handbag
marinara."

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.000
Together.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.720
Oh, God - imagine how their kids would turn
out!

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.420
On some level it made sense, because they
were the two friends who dated around the

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:01.920
most.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.440
On every other level, it made no sense, because
there had never been any heat between those

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.440
two characters.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.000
It was just weird, and before long Rachel
and Joey realized they were meant to be - surprise!

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.140
- friends, rendering the whole plot arc an
exercise in wheel-spinning.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.560
Oh well - at least it spawned some of our
favorite Gunther moments.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.000
"Rachel?!"

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.040
Oh How I met your mother...

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.420
You had so much potential.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.070
You could've gone down as one of the most
consistent sitcoms of all time - were it not

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.760
for that last season, of course.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:35.280
Sure, fans eventually learned that the woman
of Ted's dreams was a gal named Tracy - but

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.380
the actual finale of the show found him middle-aged
and rekindling his romance with friend and

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.880
fellow main character Robin.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.800
The show's provocative thesis?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.540
A person can have two great loves in their
life.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:51.700
If you're wondering where the hell all that
came from - well, so were a lot of viewers.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.980
The harsh reality is: How I Met Your Mother
wasted most of its final season, which takes

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.380
place mostly in the hours leading up to the
wedding of Robin and Barney.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.060
So much time was spent puttering around that
the finale episode crammed in a ton of stories

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.920
and the passage of many years that could have
been explored in depth over the course of

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.420
the season.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.780
These briefly mentioned things include Ted
and Tracy getting to know each other, having

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.770
their kids, Tracy dying, and how Barney and
Robin get divorced.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.240
So, you know, the stuff that would have actually
made us care.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.540
Instead, we got…

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:31.060
"Everything I have and everything I am is
yours."

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.140
Oof.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.880
Way to drop the ball and pull a Lost, guys.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.980
Dexter dared to go where no other show had
dared go before: It was a series where the

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.840
protagonist was a serial killer.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:47.560
The writers actually got viewers to root for
a man consumed by his desire to murder - and

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:51.920
they made him a sympathetic character because
he only really ever killed really bad people.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:52.600
Usually.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:57.860
Dexter really made good use of its home on
Showtime, depicting graphic murders and mutilations

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.080
and whatnot, desensitizing fans over time
to all of that horrific and violent imagery.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.540
Where could a show like that possibly go after
that?

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:05.420
Incest!

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.840
One of Dexter's few allies in the world was
his sister, Debra, a Miami homicide detective.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.550
In the show's sixth season finale, Debra not
only finds out her brother is a serial killer,

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.400
but realizes that she loves him…

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:18.300
romantically.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:23.400
He's technically her adoptive brother, but
still - that's almost as hard to stomach as,

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.120
well…

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.900
"You are the love of my life."

